0..78 Comment "// Order through the prelude\'s `Ord` (#2333): `<`, `<=`, `>` and `>=` call the"
79..153 Comment "// prelude\'s `lt`, `le`, `gt` and `ge`, whose model of `Ord` the operands\'"
154..222 Comment "// type resolves. `OrdInteger` answers the integers with the integer"
223..300 Comment "// primitives, so their verdicts are the primitives\'; `OrdString` answers the"
301..376 Comment "// strings byte by byte, the order a Rust `BTreeMap<String, _>` keeps. Each"
377..436 Comment "// includes its `Eq` model, so `==` still resolves at both."
